<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
    Debug-only entitlements for DynaMoE: intentionally empty.

    The Release build adds keychain-access-groups (DynaMoE-Release.entitlements)
    so it can use the data protection keychain. That entitlement is restricted:
    Xcode has to resolve a Developer ID provisioning profile for the build, and
    a build that carries it without a matching profile is killed at launch. Local
    development should not pay either cost, so Debug keeps no keychain group and
    SecretStoreSupport falls back to the legacy login keychain exactly as every
    earlier version did.

    To exercise the data protection path from a local build, sign it with the
    Release entitlements and the embedded profile instead of changing this file.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict/>
</plist>
